B net-debt figure used instead).\n\nKEY CONCLUSION (foreshadow)\n\u2022 Base-case intrinsic value \u2248 $118/share (WACC 9.3%, terminal g 4.0%).\n\u2022 Scenario-expected value \u2248 $129/share. Price $157.01 \u2192 MoS \u221217.8% \u2192 NONE.\n\u2022 The market is paying for the bull-ish AI path. Verdict: HOLD existing;\n  NO new position at T0; accumulate $115-125; trim discipline >$175.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSTEP 1-1. MACRO VARIABLES (as of most recent retrievable data; tags reflect source)\n\u2022 10Y UST: 4.65%, up from 4.30% a year earlier \u2014 rates ELEVATED and RISING.\n  [Actual - ycharts, Aug 2026]\n\u2022 Real 10Y: ~1.6-1.9% (4.65% less core CPI ~2.9%) [Estimate].\n\u2022 Fed policy: rate-cut hopes cooled through 2026 (sticky inflation delaying\n  easing); policy effectively neutral-to-restrictive. [Estimate - ironfx 2026]\n\u2022 DXY: Morgan Stanley sees ~94 by Q2 2026 \u2014 mild dollar softness. [Estimate]\n\u2022 Liquidity/risk appetite: VIX 15.55, S&P 7,669, gold $4,700, WTI $82 \u2014\n  risk-on but late-cycle pricing. [Actual - market data via Yahoo, Aug 2026]\n\u2022 Economic cycle: late expansion; AI-capex investment boom is the marginal\n  growth engine; inflation above target; credit spreads benign [Unconfirmed \u2014\n  no direct spread series retrieved; inferred from VIX level].\n\u2022 Commodities: Goldman 2026 copper avg forecast raised to ~$11,400/t [Estimate \u2014\n  capital.com]. Copper inflation is a cost-push input for APH (largely pass-through).\n\nSTEP 1-2. REGIME PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION (must sum to 100%)\n\u2022 Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 25%\n\u2022 Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%  \u2190 modal regime (AI boom + 4.65% 10Y)\n\u2022 Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 20%\n\u2022 Recession (low rates + low growth): 20%\nRationale: the 10Y at 4.65% rules out a classical Goldilocks; the AI capex boom\n(growth) with sticky rates maps to Reflation; Stagflation/Recession tails priced\nfor an AI-capex peak followed by a growth stall.\n\nSTEP 1-3. APH MACRO SENSITIVITY (each \u22123 to +3)\n\u2022 Interest rates: \u22121.5 (long-duration growth multiple; leverage up post-CCS)\n\u2022 Dollar: \u22120.5 (global sales, USD costs; mild translation/competition effect)\n\u2022 Liquidity: +2.0 (AI datacom capex is financing-sensitive \u2014 direct beneficiary)\n\u2022 Economic cycle: +1.5 (datacom/defense strength offsets soft auto/industrial)\n\u2022 Commodities: \u22120.5 (copper cost inflation, mostly passed through)\n\nSTEP 1-4. MACRO ALIGNMENT\nExpected macro impact = 0.25(+1.5) + 0.35(+1.0) + 0.20(\u22120.5) + 0.20(\u22122.0)\n                      = +0.225 \u2192 NEUTRAL (slight tailwind). No conviction change.\nMacro does not alter intrinsic value; it only informs entry timing (see S.12).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250