ION OPINION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nACTION: HOLD / DO NOT INITIATE. (No \"Buy\" at $157.01.)\n\u2022 Amphenol is a best-in-class quality compounder (wide moat 14/21, ROIC ~25%,\n  ROE 38%, FCF conversion 80%+, 11/15 capital allocation) \u2014 the business\n  deserves a premium multiple. The PRICE, however, embeds the bull-ish AI path:\n  at $157 the market is ~17-25% above my scenario-expected ($129) and base ($118)\n  intrinsic values, with no margin of safety and a negative Kelly edge.\n\u2022 CONVICTION: 12/15 (High \u2014 quality), ENTRY conviction LOW (valuation).\n\u2022 WEIGHT: New money 0-2% (tactical only); existing holders \u2264 5% target, trim\n  ~20-25% of position into strength > $175-180; core holders may HOLD through\n  the AI cycle given business quality, accepting ~20% tail risk to $90-100.\n\u2022 STRATEGY:\n  \u2022 Add zone: $115-125 (\u2248 base IV \u00b1 1\u03c3; 0.5x starter, 1.0x full at < $118 if\n    thesis KPIs intact: book-to-bill > 1.0, margins > 24%, CCS > 15%).\n  \u2022 No-touch zone: $150-180 (overvalued; let the AI momentum run without\n    chasing; harvest on spikes > $175).\n  \u2022 Trim/exit triggers: IT datacom organic < 10% YoY; book-to-bill < 1.0 for 2\n    quarters; adj op margin < 24%; hyperscaler capex guidance cuts; net\n    debt/EBITDA > 2.0x; CCS impairment.\n  \u2022 Monitoring cadence: quarterly post-earnings, thesis-KPI checklist (S.8).\n\u2022 EXPECTED RETURN IF ENTERED AT $120: (129\u2212120)/120 \u2248 +7.5% + 0.6% div over\n  ~3-4 yrs \u2192 ~2.5-3.5%/yr \u2014 modest; this is a qualit