ood).\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:\n- Revenue CAGR (5-yr): 21.9% [Actual \u2014 filing-derived]\n- Operating margin: TTM 25.4% [Arithmetic]; Q2'26 29.5% GAAP / 29.8% adjusted\n  [Actual]\n- ROE: 38.1% [Aggregator]\n- ROIC: \u2248 27% [Estimate \u2014 NOPAT ~7.9B / (equity 13.5B + net debt 4.1B)]\n- FCF margin: TTM 16.3%; FY25 18.9% [Arithmetic]\n- FCF conversion: FY25 101.7% [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt / EBITDA: net debt ~$4.1B / EBITDA ~$6.8B \u2248 0.6x [Estimate]\n- Interest coverage: FY26E OI $10.4B / interest $0.55B \u2248 19x [Estimate]\n- Structure: net debt small, investment grade [Assumption \u2014 no rating retrieved]\nJudgment: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard:\n1. Buyback efficiency: 1/3 (Q2'26 buyback $208M only; share count rising ~1%/yr\n   on M&A-related issuance [Actual \u2014 FY24\u2192FY25 weighted shares 1,263.6M\u21921,277.5M])\n2. M&A track record: 3/3 (CommScope raised from $4.1B/$0.15 to $4.6B/$0.30\n   [Actual \u2014 company IR]; 12-yr history without major impairment)\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 (capex 4.3% of sales, incremental ROIC >>20%)\n4. Rationality of mix: 2/3 (accretive M&A + dividends, small buybacks \u2014 fine,\n   but no big undervalued repurchases)\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 (Q1'26 and Q2'26 both exceeded high end [Actual])\nSubtotal 12/15. Insider: CEO owns ~2.8M shares post-sale (~0.23%) \u2192 no +1 for\n>5% ownership; no 6-mo net buy; 6-mo LARGE net SELL (CEO sold 686,104 shares,\n~$111M, 7/31/26 [Actual \u2014 SEC Form 4 via Yahoo]) \u2192 -2.\nFinal score: 10/15.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25