om IT datacom [Estimate] means a large AI-cycle sensitivity,\nbut revenue is real and current (not future optionality), so Engine 4 (option-led)\nwould mis-price current earnings. (3) Engine 2 (cycle-adjusted) is used as a\ncross-check because AI capex is cyclical. (4) Not in archetype transition;\nit is a compounder experiencing an accelerated growth phase.\n\nStep 3-1. Forecast (all dollars B, fiscal years; FY ends Dec):\n\n| FY    | Rev | Growth  | OpMgn | OI    | NI    | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC  | FCFF |\n|-------|-----|---------|-------|-------|-------|-----|-------|------|------|\n| 2026E | 35.7| +54.6%  | 29.2% | 10.43 | 7.50  | 1.43| 1.53  | 0    | 7.82 |\n| 2027E | 42.8| +20.0%  | 29.5% | 12.63 | 9.20  | 1.71| 1.84  | -0.20| 9.29 |\n| 2028E | 47.9| +12.0%  | 29.5% | 14.13 | 10.30 | 1.92| 2.06  | -0.15| 10.43|\n| 2029E | 50.8| +6.0%   | 29.0% | 14.73 | 10.42 | 2.03| 2.18  | -0.05| 10.64|\n| 2030E | 54.4| +7.0%   | 29.2% | 15.88 | 11.42 | 2.18| 2.34  | 0    | 11.68|\n\nDriver sourcing (mandated by rules):\n- FY2026 revenue: Q1 $7.620B [Actual], Q2 $8.758B [Actual], Q3 guide $9.3-9.4B\n  (mid $9.35B) [Actual \u2014 company guidance], Q4 estimate $10.0B [Estimate \u2014\n  sequential +7% based on FY24 Q4/Q3 +6.9% and FY25 Q4/Q3 +4.0%, plus B2B 1.23].\n- FY27 growth +20%: [Estimate] \u2014 hyperscaler capex still accelerating (~$900B\n  2026E top-7, ~$1.5T 2027E [Estimate \u2014 Facebook/24-7 Wall St summary of\n  consensus]; UBS $4.1T cumulative 2026-28 [Estimate \u2014 24-7 Wall St]); APH IT\n  datacom 41% of sales [Estimate]; offset by non-datacom ~5% and no further\n  CommScope inorganic step-up.\n- FY28 +12%, FY29 +6%, FY30 +7%: [Assumption] \u2014 deliberately descending\n  from +20% as AI capex growth normalizes. NOT company guidance. Post-FY27\n  growth is unguided and is the single largest uncertainty; scenario band\n  covers -20% to +30% in the bear/bull cases.\n- Op margin: FY26 29.2% [Estimate] \u2014 Q2'26 adj 29.8% [Actual] includes $80M\n  one-time