\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nSECTION 0. ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nIDENTITY\n\u2022 APH, Electronic Components (Technology). Fiscal year ends 2025-12-31.\n\u2022 T0 price $157.01 [Actual - vendor quote 2026-08-24]; market cap $193.53B on\n  1,232.6M vendor shares [Aggregator]. Diluted share base ~1.30B used for\n  per-share math [Estimate - FY2025 filed diluted 1,277.5M + 0.3%/yr SBC drift].\n\u2022 Enterprise value: $206.93B = $193.53B + net debt $13.4B [Actual - company\n  disclosure 2026-06-30: total debt $18.8B, net debt $13.4B, liquidity $8.4B].\n\nENTERPRISE CLASSIFICATION (Layer 0)\n\u2022 Archetype: B \u2014 Quality Compounder, WITH a documented cyclical-flavor overlay.\n  Three reasons: (1) 10-yr revenue CAGR +21.9% with revenue never falling more\n  than ~0.5% in any pack year (FY2019 \u22120.3%, FY2023 \u22120.5%) \u2014 this is not the\n  signature of a pure Cyclical; (2) ROE 38.1%, ROIC ~24-26%, op margin 25.4%\n  latest vs 20.4% 10-yr median \u2014 a classic quality compounder profile; (3) the\n  growth engine is M&A plus AI-content share gains, not a single-commodity cycle.\n\u2022 Transition watch: IT datacom is now 43% of quarterly sales (+89% YoY, 63%\n  organic) [Estimate - company call via aggregator]. This is a structural\n  increase in AI-cycle exposure. APH is drifting toward Archetype C on the\n  concentration dimension \u2014 I treat this inside the scenario engine (widened\n  bear tail) rather than re-classifying, because margins and the M&A engine\n  remain quality-compounder-like. Re-classify to C if IT datacom > 50% of sales\n  AND organic growth turns negative in a datacom digestion.\n\u2022 Engine selected: ENGINE 1 (Traditional DCF + Multiples), with explicit\n  cycle-aware scenarios and an Engine 4 (reverse-DCF) cross-check.\n  Why not Engine 2: APH's normalized earnings do not swing with a single\n  industry cycle; why not Engine 4: <10% of value should come from binary\n  optionality \u2014 the AI ramp is already in the base revenue base (IT datacom 43%\n  of sales is realized revenue, not optionality).\n\nDATA RELIABILITY NOTES (applied before any number is used)\n\u2022 Pack FY2025 revenue step 12.555\u219223.095B (+84%): verified NOT a basis change.\n  Q2 2026 call confirms +55% USD / +30% organic with CommScope CCS (~$4.6B 2026\n  sales) consolidating [Actual - company call]. Treat as real acquisition + real\n  AI organic growth.\n\u2022 Share count 2022\u21922023 (621.0M\u21921,241.2M): 2-for-1 split, not issuance.\n\u2022 Vendor trailing P/E 42.60 implies EPS ~$3.69, which matches NO pack figure\n  (TTM NI/share $4.06 on diluted; FY2025 $3.37). Unresolved vendor-period\n  inconsistency \u2014 pack TTM figures used instead. [Unconfirmed]\n\u2022 Pack FY2025 \"change in WC +$7.86B\" is dominated by the cash build from\n  acquisition debt and is UNUSABLE in a DCF; operating-WC behavior inferred\n  from OCF \u2248 NI + D&A (FY2025: OCF $5.375B vs NI+D&A $5.227B; gap +0.148B\n  \u2192 working-capital-neutral business). [Estimate]\n\u2022 Net debt: pack FY2025-based estimate ($4.6B) is SUPERSEDED by the 6/30/26\n  disclosure of $13.4B net debt after the debt-funded CCS close. [Actual]\n  Components: LT noncurrent + current portion verified additive against vendor\n  total debt $15.502B (14.565 + 0.937 = 15.502) \u2713; operating leases $0.566B\n  (FY2025) excluded from the vendor scalar, included in my quality screens but\n  NOT in the EV bridge (company's own $13.4B net-debt figure used instead).\n\nKEY CONCLUSION (foreshadow)\n\u2022 Base-case intrinsic value \u2248 $118/share (WACC 9.3%, terminal g 4.0%).\n\u2022 Scenario-expected value \u2248 $129/share. Price $157.01 \u2192 MoS \u221217.8% \u2192 NONE.\n\u2022 The market is paying for the bull-ish AI path. Verdict: HOLD existing;\n  NO new position at T0; accumulate $115-125; trim discipline >$175.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSTEP 1-1. MACRO VARIABLES (as of most recent retrievable data; tags reflect source)\n\u2022 10Y UST: 4.65%, up from 4.30% a year earlier \u2014 rates ELEVATED and RISING.\n  [Actual - ycharts, Aug 2026]\n\u2022 Real 10Y: ~1.6-1.9% (4.65% less core CPI ~2.9%) [Estimate].\n\u2022 Fed policy: rate-cut hopes cooled through 2026 (sticky inflation delaying\n  easing); policy effectively neutral-to-restrictive. [Estimate - ironfx 2026]\n\u2022 DXY: Morgan Stanley sees ~94 by Q2 2026 \u2014 mild dollar softness. [Estimate]\n\u2022 Liquidity/risk appetite: VIX 15.55, S&P 7,669, gold $4,700, WTI $82 \u2014\n  risk-on but late-cycle pricing. [Actual - market data via Yahoo, Aug 2026]\n\u2022 Economic cycle: late expansion; AI-capex investment boom is the marginal\n  growth engine; inflation above target; credit spreads benign [Unconfirmed \u2014\n  no direct spread series retrieved; inferred from VIX level].\n\u2022 Commodities: Goldman 2026 copper avg forecast raised to ~$11,400/t [Estimate \u2014\n  capital.com]. Copper inflation is a cost-push input for APH (largely pass-through).\n\nSTEP 1-2. REGIME PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION (must sum to 100%)\n\u2022 Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 25%\n\u2022 Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%  \u2190 modal regime (AI boom + 4.65% 10Y)\n\u2022 Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 20%\n\u2022 Recession (low rates + low growth): 20%\nRationale: the 10Y at 4.65% rules out a classical Goldilocks; the AI capex boom\n(growth) with sticky rates maps to Reflation; Stagflation/Recession tails priced\nfor an AI-capex peak followed by a growth stall.\n\nSTEP 1-3. APH MACRO SENSITIVITY (each \u22123 to +3)\n\u2022 Interest rates: \u22121.5 (long-duration growth multiple; leverage up post-CCS)\n\u2022 Dollar: \u22120.5 (global sales, USD costs; mild translation/competition effect)\n\u2022 Liquidity: +2.0 (AI datacom capex is financing-sensitive \u2014 direct beneficiary)\n\u2022 Economic cycle: +1.5 (datacom/defense strength offsets soft auto/industrial)\n\u2022 Commodities: \u22120.5 (copper cost inflation, mostly passed through)\n\nSTEP 1-4. MACRO ALIGNMENT\nExpected macro impact = 0.25(+1.5) + 0.35(+1.0) + 0.20(\u22120.5) + 0.20(\u22122.0)\n                      = +0.225 \u2192 NEUTRAL (slight tailwind). No conviction change.\nMacro does not alter intrinsic value; it only informs entry timing (see S.12).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nSECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSTEP 1.5-1. BASE RATES APPLICABLE TO APH\n\u2022 5-yr survival of a >20%-ROIC, wide-moat large-cap industrial: ~95% [base rate].\n\u2022 Probability a mega-cap industrial grows revenue >10% for 5 years AFTER a\n  +50% growth year: ~30-40% (growth mean-reverts at scale) [base rate].\n\u2022 Hyperscaler capex growing >20% for a 5th consecutive year (2027): ~55-65%\n  (capex cycles historically peak after 3-5 years of expansion) [Assumption].\n\u2022 $10.5B M&A (CCS) delivering ROIC > WACC within 5 years: ~25-35% base rate;\n  APH's own historical M&A hit-rate is above base (~50-60% by track record),\n  but CCS is unproven at 2 quarters \u2014 use ~40% blended [Assumption].\n\nSTEP 1.5-2. DEVIATION FROM BASE RATE \u2014 REQUIRED JUSTIFICATIONS\nMy base case assumes FY2027-30 revenue CAGR ~12% and 27-28% near-term margins.\nThat is ~1.3-1.5\u00d7 the base rate for a $36B-revenue company \u2014 near the 1.5x flag.\nThree company-specific justifications for the deviation:\n1. Order evidence: record Q2 orders $10.732B, book-to-bill 1.23:1, every end\n   market positive; Q3 2026 guided +50-52% YoY [Actual - company call].\n2. Secular content shift: IT datacom +89% YoY (63% organic), 43% of sales, and\n   management guidance of ANOTHER mid-teens sequential increase in Q3 \u2014 the AI\n   interconnect content per server is rising, not a one-time pull-in [Actual].\n3. Hyperscaler capex visibility: Morgan Stanley forecasts $805B (2026) \u2192\n   $1.116T (2027) for AMZN/MSFT/GOOGL/META/ORCL; Goldman $1.15T 2025-27 vs\n   $477B 2022-24 \u2014 a visible multi-year demand envelope for high-speed\n   interconnect [Estimate - sell-side].\nConclusion: deviation is justified for the near term (2026-27) but NOT for\n2028+. I therefore fade growth to ~8.5% by FY2030 and 4% terminal \u2014 the\nbase-rate discipline is imposed on the outer years.\n\nSTEP 1.5-3. BASE-RATE SHOCK CHECK\n\u2022 Implied success probability in my bull/base mix vs base rate: base-case\n  revenue CAGR 12% vs base ~9-10% for a company with APH's historical franchise\n  \u2192 ratio ~1.2-1.3x \u2192 evidence filed above (orders, capex) \u2192 PASS, no red flag.\n\u2022 The bear case (25%) explicitly re-applies the mean-reversion base rate.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (Buffett + Lynch)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSTEP 2-1. UNDERSTANDING\nAmphenol designs and manufactures electrical, electronic and fiber-optic\nconnectors, interconnect systems, cable assemblies and sensors sold across IT\ndatacom, defense, industrial, automotive, mobile devices and comm networks.\nIt operates ~100+ decentralized divisions, competing on engineering breadth and\nqualification speed in a fragmented global market. Understandability: HIGH\n(tangible product, visible demand drivers, readable financials).\n\nSTEP 2-2. MOAT SCORE (0-3 each, total /21)\n\u2022 Intangible assets (brand/engineering IP): 2   \u2022 Switching costs: 3\n\u2022 Network effects: 1                              \u2022 Cost advantage: 2\n\u2022 Economies of scale: 3                           \u2022 Regulatory barriers: 2\n\u2022 Data moat: 1\nTOTAL: 14/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT.\nDirection: WIDENING near-term (AI content per device rising, share gains in\nhigh-speed copper/optics/power, CommScope scale) with a narrowing WATCH-ITEM in\nAI interconnect (Luxshare/TE/Molex capacity build, commoditization of passive\nassemblies). Net: Widening with an expiry date on the AI premium \u2014 reflected in\nthe margin fade in the DCF.\n\nSTEP 2-3. LYNCH CLASSIFICATION\nFast Grower (transitioned from Stalwart). Checkpoints: PEG ~1.1 [Estimate];\ngrowth sustainability \u2014 YES near-term (orders, guide), UNPROVEN beyond 2027;\nearnings quality \u2014 high (accruals ratio \u22120.037, OCF\u2248NI+D&A); balance sheet \u2014\nadequate after CCS (net debt/EBITDA ~1.2x, coverage ~10x).\n\nSTEP 2-4. FINANCIAL STRENGTH SCORECARD (FY2025 [Actual] unless noted)\n\u2022 Revenue CAGR 3-yr (FY22-25): +22.3%; last-4Q growth +55% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Op margin: 25.4% latest vs 20.4% 10-yr median\n\u2022 EPS growth: FY24\u2192FY25 +39% (2.442\u21924.305B NI, diluted shares +1.1%)\n\u2022 ROE 38.1% [Aggregator]; ROIC ~24-26% [Estimate, see 2.5]\n\u2022 FCF margin 19.0% (FY25), 16.2% (TTM); FCF/OCF conversion 81% (FY25)\n\u2022 Net debt $13.4B [Actual 6/30/26]; net debt/EBITDA ~1.2x (FY26E); coverage ~10x\n\u2022 Net-cash-vs-debt: structurally NET DEBT now (was near-net-cash pre-CCS)\nJUDGMENT: EXCELLENT (leverage step-up is the one qualification).\n\nSTEP 2-5. CAPITAL ALLOCATION SCORECARD (0-3 each; total /15)\n1. Buyback efficiency: 2 \u2014 1.5M shares @ $141 in Q2 2026 (~$212M) [Actual];\n   modest, disciplined, not peak-aggressive.\n2. M&A track record: 2 \u2014 historical ROIC > WACC consistently; CCS $10.5B\n   [Actual - IR] unproven; accretion outlook DOUBLED to $0.30 within 2 quarters\n   [Actual - call] \u2014 encouraging but early.\n3. Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 capex only ~4% of sales with 24%+ incremental ROIC.\n4. Rationality of mix: 3 \u2014 reinvestment + bolt-ons + buybacks + dividend\n   (~$515M capital returned in Q2 alone) [Actual].\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 \u2014 beat high end in Q1 AND Q2 2026 [Actual].\nBASE: 13/15. Insider adjustment: CEO discretionary sales (NOT 10b5-1) of ~$76M\n(Feb 2026) + ~$18.7M (May 2026) [Estimate - aggregator Form-4 reports] \u2192 \u22122.\nFINAL: 11/15. Strength: excellent allocator; watch-item: insider selling timing.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n2.5-1 R&D capitalization: APH R&D not in pack; real-world scale ~3.5% of\nrevenue [Assumption - not retrievable, [Unconfirmed] as filed]. Capitalizing\nFY2025 R&D (~$0.81B) at 5-yr amortization adds ~$0.5B to NOPAT and ~$2.4B to\ninvested capital \u2192 adjusted ROIC ~25.5% vs GAAP ~24.5% (gap < 5pp \u2192 no\nmaterial distortion; APH is an engineering-light, assembly-heavy business).\n2.5-2 SBC treatment: FY2025 SBC $0.135B [Actual] = 0.6% of revenue. Adjusted\nFCF = reported FCF 4.378 \u2212 SBC 0.135 = $4.24B. SBC already expensed in OI, so\nmy FCFF (below) is NOT double-counted. Negligible per-share distortion.\n2.5-3 Operating leases: $0.566B (FY2025) [Actual]. Included in leverage screen;\nadjusted net debt $13.97B; coverage still >9x. Immaterial.\n2.5-4 Brand/data assets: not meaningful for a component manufacturer \u2014 skipped.\n2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC: ~25.5% vs GAAP ~24.5% \u2192 no >5pp gap \u2192 GAAP adequate here.\n2.5-6 Owner earnings (FY2025): NI 4.305 + D&A 0.922 \u2212 maintenance capex ~0.55\n\u2212 \u0394WC ~0.05 \u2248 $4.63B [Estimate]. \u2248 reported FCF $4.378B. Confirms cash quality.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nSECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES; + reverse-DCF cross-check)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDISCOUNT-RATE DERIVATION (all inputs sourced or tagged)\n\u2022 Risk-free: 4.65% \u2014 10Y UST, Aug 2026 [Actual - ycharts].\n\u2022 ERP: 4.75% [Assumption - Damodaran-style long-run, 4.5-5.0% band].\n\u2022 Beta: 1.10 [Estimate \u2014 vendor 1.251 [Aggregator] vs long-run APH ~1.0; blended\n  upward for post-CCS leverage]. Levered check: unlevered ~0.95 \u00d7 (1 + 0.755\u00d7\n  (18.8/193.5)) \u2248 1.02 \u2014 1.10 is a reasonable, slightly conservative input.\n\u2022 Cost of equity = 4.65% + 1.10 \u00d7 4.75% = 9.88%.\n\u2022 Pre-tax cost of debt: 5.25% [Assumption - A-rated industrial, 10Y + ~60bp];\n  after-tax (24.5%) = 3.96%.\n\u2022 Weights: debt $18.8B (gross) / $212.3B (D+E) = 8.9%; equity 91.1%.\n\u2022 WACC = 0.911\u00d79.88% + 0.089\u00d73.96% = 9.35% \u2192 BASE WACC 9.3% (sensitivity 8.8-9.8%).\n\nFORECAST DRIVERS \u2014 every line sourced\n\u2022 Revenue FY2026 $36.0B: H1 actual $16.378B [Actual] + Q3 guide $9.3-9.4B\n  [Actual - mgmt] + Q4 ~$10.0B (sequential +6-8% on 1.23 book-to-bill, IT\n  datacom mid-teens sequential) [Estimate]. = +56% YoY.\n\u2022 Revenue FY2027 $42.1B (+17%): consensus forward revenue growth 16.98%\n  [Aggregator - yfinance]; cross-checked against brief's \"low-to-mid teens\"\n  [Estimate]. CCS contributes ~$4.6B full year [Actual - raised outlook].\n\u2022 FY2028 +12% ($47.2B), FY2029 +10% ($51.9B), FY2030 +8.5% ($56.3B):\n  MY DECELERATION ASSUMPTION [Assumption] \u2014 fade from consensus-anchored +17%\n  toward APH's long-run organic 6-8% + M&A 2-3%; NOT established by any\n  guidance (pack guidance covers FY2026 only). Shown explicitly so the reader\n  can stress it: a \u00b12pp change in FY28-30 CAGR moves IV by roughly \u00b1$6-8.\n\u2022 Operating margin: FY2026 27.5% (Q2 adjusted 29.8%, ex-tariff ~29% [Actual -\n  call]; Q1 depresse