hs.\n5. CEO sold ~$95M of stock in 2026, discretionarily, outside 10b5-1 plans \u2014\n   insiders monetizing the +71.7% run.\n6. Customer concentration rising: hyperscaler procurement power + Chinese\n   competitor capacity = margin compression with a lag.\n7. Copper at ~$11,400/t and IEEPA tariff regimes add cost volatility exactly as\n   pricing power peaks.\nLOGIC COMBAT: Long thesis strength 6/10 (quality, moat, momentum are real);\nShort thesis strength 6/10 (valuation, concentration, insider signals are real).\nGap < 2 \u2192 per framework, CONVICTION DOWNGRADE APPLIED to the ENTRY decision\n(not to quality assessment) \u2192 no new position at T0.\nADVERSARIAL DATA: CEO sales reported by investing.com / MarketBeat [Estimate];\nUSTR remediation order re: Amphenol Optimize M\u00e9xico [Actual]; the brief's\n\"HOLD\" downgrade note [Unconfirmed].\nKILLED ARGUMENTS (conditions under which they revive):\n\u2022 \"APH has compounded 15% for 30 years, therefore it will continue\" \u2014 KILLED\n  as an entry argument by 43% AI concentration; REVIVES only if FY2027 organic\n  growth > 10% with book-to-bill > 1.0.\n\u2022 \"AI is secular, not cyclical\" \u2014 KILLED by every historical capex cycle;\n  REVIVES only if hyperscaler capex keeps growing > 20% into 2028.\n\u2022 \"Insider selling is just diversification\" \u2014 KILLED by the absence of 10b5-1\n  plans and the clustering; REVIVES if selling stops and insiders buy.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (37-point, summarized; all pass)\n\u2022 A. Methodology: DCF + multiples + reverse-DCF + scenarios; no single-engine\n  conclusion \u2713. \u2022 B. Valuation: g=4% \u2264 nominal GDP; WACC derived from current\n  10Y 4.65% \u2713; margin path ABOVE history is explicitly assumption-tagged \u2713.\n\u2022 C. Bias: overconfidence check \u2014 near-term margins 27.5-28% are above the 10-yr\n  median; bear case applies reversion; insider red flag included \u2713.\n\u2022 D. Consistency: FY2026 $36.0B consistent with H1 a