+10% to $30.4B | 19%\u219215%\u219214%\u219216% | $56 |\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian update:\nPrior (base rates): Bull 20%, Base 40%, Bear 30%, Severe 10%.\nEvidence since: Q2'26 B2B 1.23 (record), orders +94% YoY, CommScope guidance\nraised again ($4.6B/$0.30), Q3 guidance above consensus, but CEO sold $111M.\nPosterior: Bull \u2191 25%, Base stays 40%, Bear \u2193 25%, Severe stays 10%.\n(Insider sale is a risk flag, not a strategy signal.)\n\nStep 4-4/5. Expected value and MoS:\nEV = 0.25\u00d7187 + 0.40\u00d7145 + 0.25\u00d799 + 0.10\u00d756 = 46.75 + 58.0 + 24.75 + 5.6 =\n$135.1 \u2192 round $135/share [Estimate].\n50% confidence interval: $99-$187. 80% confidence interval: $56-$187.\nExpected drawdown CVaR (10%): -62%. Expected loss in Bear: -37%.\nMoS Base = (145-157)/145 = -8.3% \u2192 NONE.\nMoS EV = (135-157)/135 = -16.3% \u2192 NONE.\nJudgment: stock is pricing in a materially better-than-expected path.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE  [Layer 4.5]\n\nMarket-implied horizon: reverse DCF on $157 implies ~6-7 years of double-digit\nFCF growth at 8.8-9.3% discount, versus my 40%-probable base case of 5 years\nof elevated growth then normalization. Spread = my 3-5y horizon vs market's\nimplied 6-7y = 1-2 years. A 2-year spread is near the threshold where time-\narbitrage becomes meaningful; here it signals RICHNESS, not an opportunity.\nNo positive horizon arbitrage. [Estimate]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING  [Layer 5]\n\nStep 5-1. Conviction score (/15):\n1. Business quality: 3/3 (wide + widening moat, excellent financials)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 1/3 (base IV below price; EV IV well below)\n3. Macro alignment: 2/3 (AI capex tailwind vs high-rate headwind = neutral)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3/3 (KPIs: book-to-bill, IT datacom growth, CCS accretion)\n5. Execution traceability: 2/3 (12-year record excellent; insider sale a flag)\nTOTAL = 11/15 \u2192 HIGH conviction.\nStep 5-2. Conviction decay: -1 pt every 6 months without confirming evidence;\nre-evaluate on each earnings print. Step 5-3. Max weight for High conviction\n(4-8%) but Macro NEUTRAL and negative MoS forces the bottom of the band:\nMAX 4%. Because EV MoS is negative, NEW positions = 0%; existing positions \u22643%.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING  [Layer 5.5]\n\n- Short interest: 15.4M shares, 1.41% of float, 2.09 days to cover, MoM -3.6%\n  [Aggregator] \u2192 NO squeeze setup. Neutral.\n- Institutional ownership 98.2% [Aggregator] \u2192 extremely crowded on the long\n  side; any negative surprise de-risks hard. Passive/ETF flows are the swing\n  factor. Warning.\n- Insider: CEO sold $111M on 7/31/26 [Actual \u2014 Form 4] \u2192 large net sell.\n  Insider ownership 0.47% \u2192 misalignment risk.\n- Options positioning: not retrieved \u2192 [Unconfirmed].\n- Sentiment: sell-side mean target $198, low $170 [Aggregator]; each beat\n  extends the momentum-chasing. Zacks \"Hold\" downgrade noted in brief\n  [Unconfirmed]. Sentiment is at the optimistic end.\n- Crowding risk score: 12/15 (HIGH). Apply -1%p position cap.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT  [Layer 6]\n\nAPH at a 0.6x net-debt/EBITDA, FCF-positive, 29% operating margin profile is a\nQUALITY compounder with a beta \u22481.0-1.25; it provides portfolio ballast relative\nto pure AI semis but is NOT a defensive holding (IT datacom is 41% of sales).\nPortfolio fit: MODERATE. If the portfolio already has exposure to AI\ninfrastructure (NVDA, AVGO, VRT, etc.), APH adds correlation, not diversification.\nIn a 10-stock portfolio: acceptable as 3-4% position ONLY after trimming other\nAI names. In a 20+ stock portfolio: acceptable up to 4%.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING  [Layer 6.5]\n\nOutcome set (price-relative to $157):\nBull: +19.1% (187/157-1) @25%\nBase: -7.6% (145/157-1) @40%\nBear: -36.9% (99/157-1) @25%\nSevere: -64.3% (56/157-1) @10%\nExpected return = 0.25\u00d70.191 + 0.40\u00d7(-0.076) + 0.25\u00d7(-0.369) + 0.10\u00d7(-0.643)\n= 0.0478 - 0.0304 - 0.0923 - 0.0643 = -0.139 \u2192 -13.9% expected return.\nFull-Kelly = edge/odds \u2248 negative \u2192 KELLY = 0%. Fractional Kelly (25%) = 0%.\nGap check vs Layer 5 (0-3% vs 0%): gap < 20pp \u2192 no re-analysis needed.\nVERDICT: No new position. Disciplined Kelly says the probability-weighted\nrisk/reward is negative at T0.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS  [Layer 7]\n\nCatalysts (next 12 months):\n- Q3'26 print (late Oct'26): guide $9.3-9.4B; likely beat as in prior quarters.\n- Hyperscaler 2027 capex guidance (Oct-Dec'26 earnings): THE swing factor for\n  FY27 growth.\n- CommScope/CCS integration: achievement of $4.6B/2026 sales and $0.30 accretion;\n  increase would be a positive surprise.\n- Additional M&A: APH's model is serial M&A; another $1-3B bolt-on likely.\n- 2-for-1 split liquidity effect (Sept'26): cosmetic, mild retail-flow positive.\n\nRisks:\n- AI capex pause/air-pocket (2027-28): the dominant risk; revenue sensitivity\n  to IT datacom is direct (41% of sales).\n- Customer concentration in datacom (top hyperscalers).\n- Technology shift: co-packaged optics / backplane optical may erode copper\n  connector content per rack [Unconfirmed\u2014directionally negative].\n- Competition: Luxshare/TE capacity adds in 2028-29 \u2192 price/margin pressure.\n- Tariff/IEEPA: Q2'26 included $80M tariff recovery (one-time, [Actual]);\n  recurrence of tariffs is a downside.\n- M&A integration: CommScope systems are large; restructuring risk.\n- CEO insider sale ($111M, July'26 [Actual]): may or may not signal confidence;\n  at minimum, it is a sentiment overhang.\n- Mexico environmental remediation (Amphenol Optimize M\u00e9xico) [Unconfirmed\u2014\n  USTR joint statement Feb'26]; liability likely modest but headline risk.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK  [Layer 7.5]\n\nCommon bear trigger across a typical AI/growth portfolio: a 2027-28 AI capex\nair-pocket + recession. APH's 10% severe scenario (IV $56) correlates strongly\nwith a drawdown in NVDA/AVGO/VRT-style names. Tail correlation during stress\n(2022 style) for industrial-tech vs growth \u2248 0.7-0.8 [Assumption].\nConditional VaR: if the 10% severe scenario occurs, expected portfolio loss =\nloss on APH (-62%) plus correlated AI names (-50% to -70%) \u2192 portfolio CVaR\nat 90% confidence \u2248 -25% to -35%. Mitigation: keep APH position \u22643% and\navoid pairing with high-beta datacom names; the weak dollar (DXY ~99) is a\npartial portfolio hedge for international revenue.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250