.0%. IV/share = $154.1 [Calculation]\nSources: Morgan Stanley hyperscaler capex >$1.1T by 2027 [Estimate \u2014\nTheTradable, retrieved]; 2026 capex ~$725B [Estimate \u2014 ValueAddVC, retrieved].\n\n3-D. Bear case (probability 20%) \u2014 AI digestion + recession:\nFY26 rev $35.0B; FY27 \u22128% ($32.2B); FY28 +4%; FY29 +5%; FY30 +5% ($37.0B).\nOp margins 26.0% \u2192 24.5%. FCF: 5.80, 6.29, 6.27, 6.54, 6.86. Terminal g 2.5%.\nIV/share = $59.5 [Calculation]\nJustification: 2023 cloud-digestion analogue; comm networks already \u22126% organic\n[Actual \u2014 transcript]; Fed hike risk; 10Y at 4.71% pressures all long-duration\ntech.\n\n3-E. Probability-weighted intrinsic value:\n0.55 \u00d7 102.6 + 0.25 \u00d7 154.1 + 0.20 \u00d7 59.5 = $106.9 \u2192 **$107** [Calculation]\n\nMargin of safety: (107 \u2212 157.01)/107 = \u221246.9% \u2192 NONE (negative).\n\n3-F. Tornado (Top 3 variables driving IV):\n1. IT datacom growth path after FY27: range $90-$130 [Assumption \u2014 \u00b1$20]\n2. WACC (9.0% to 11.0%): range $122 to $88 [Calculation]\n3. Terminal growth (2.5% to 4.5%): range $88 to $118 [Calculation]\nThese three become the thesis KPIs.\n\n3-G. Multiples cross-check:\n- Trailing P/E 42.6x [Pack \u00a78]; FY26E EPS $5.25 [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo Finance via\n  search] \u2192 29.9x; FY27E EPS $6.37 [Estimate \u2014 pack consensus +21.3%] \u2192 24.6x\n- PEG 1.17 [Pack]; P/B 13.5x; FCF yield (TTM) 2.4% [Arithmetic]\n- 10-year average forward multiple for APH: ~22-26x [Assumption \u2014 from market\n  history]. At 25x FY27 EPS 6.37 \u2192 $159 \u2014 approximately the current price.\n  The price embeds a full 25x multiple on FY27 even though FY27 is only 15\n  months forward. On my base-case FY28 EPS ($7.89 [Estimate \u2014 base NI 9.73B]),\n  the current price is 20x FY28 \u2014 paying today for 2028 earnings.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n- Competitive response (TE Connectivity, Molex, Luxshare): \u22122. All three are\n  expanding AI/copper/optical capacity; price pressure on high-speed interconnects\n  is a margin risk. Already visible in the company's decision to buy rather than\n  build in some areas.\n- Reflexivity: +1. High stock price supports SBC-based talent retention, M&A\n  currency, customer confidence; negative feedback would matter only at much\n  lower prices.\n- Customer evolution: +1. Early-adopter hyperscalers \u2192 mainstream enterprise AI\n  adoption extends the datacom cycle; late-adopter telecom (5G/6G) provides\n  second wave. But mainstream adoption is slower and price-sensitive.\nNet: \u22120 to \u22121 long-run drag on margins, captured in the fading margin path.\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nPrior (Layer 1.5): hypergrowth persistence ~35% base rate.\nUpdate triggers: Q2'26 orders +94%, book-to-bill 1.23 [Actual \u2014 raises bull];\nhyperscaler capex $725B/2026 and >$1.1T/2027 [Estimate \u2014 raises bull];\n10Y at 4.71% with hike risk ~1/3 [Actual \u2014 raises bear]; CEO insider sales\n~$196M in 6 months [Estimate \u2014 raises bear].\nPosterior: Base 55% | Bull 25% | Bear 20%.\n\nExpected 12-month price (convergence to IV is slow; use 3-yr):\nBase 3-yr IV: 102.6 \u00d7 1.10\u00b3 = $136.6 [Calculation]\nBull 3-yr IV: 154.1 \u00d7 1.10\u00b3 = $205.1 [Calculation]\nBear 3-yr IV: 59.5 \u00d7 1.10\u00b3 = $79.2 [Calculation]\nProbability-weighted 3-yr expected price = 0.55(136.6)+0.25(205.1)+0.20(79.2)\n= 75.1 + 51.3 + 15.8 = **$142.2** [Calculation]\nvs T0 $157.01 \u2192 expected 3-yr total return \u2248 \u22129.4% total, \u22123.2% annualized\n[Calculation]. With dividends (~0.6%) \u2192 \u2248 \u22122.6%/yr expected. Negative expected\nreturn.\n\nSECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\n- Market-implied horizon: price = 25x FY27 EPS; with 21% growth, the market\n  implicitly extends 20%+ growth through FY28-FY29 and then normalises at a\n  premium multiple. That is a 5-7 year high-growth horizon.\n- My horizon: 5 years, with growth fading from 54% to 6%.\n- Spread: The market prices roughly 2 additional years of 20%+ growth versus my\n  base case. Given the base rate for sustained hypergrowth (~35%), this is NOT\n  an arbitrage opportunity for the long side; it is a risk premium for holders.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nScorecard (0-15):\n1. Business quality: 5/5 (wide moat, 38% ROE, 11/15 capital allocation)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 0/5 (47% above probability-weighted IV)\n3. Macro alignment: 2/5 (neutral; weak dollar helps, 4.7% rates hurt)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3/5 (AI-datacom clear; post-2027 path unanchored)\n5. Execution traceability: 4/5 (quarterly beats; acquisition dilution muddy)\nTOTAL: 14/15 nominal. BUT the framework caps practical conviction when\nvaluation = 0/5 and expected 3-yr return is negative. I override: conviction\nfor NEW PURCHASES = LOW (4/15). Conviction in the COMPANY quality = HIGH,\nbut that is not a buy signal at this price.\nConviction decay: \u22121 every 6 months without confirming evidence of sustained\nAI demand.\n\nPosition sizing: 0% starting weight. If held, TRIM to \u22642% (halve the standard\nguideline given macro headwind \u2014 actually macro is neutral; use the negative\nexpected return as the reason). Add zone: $105-120 (where MoS \u2265 10-20% vs base\ncase).\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short interest: 1.41% of float; 15.42M shares; days to cover 2.09; MoM \u22123.6%\n  [Actual \u2014 pack \u00a79]. Very low \u2014 no squeeze fuel.\n- Institutional ownership: 98.16% [Actual \u2014 pack \u00a79]. Crowded. Passive/ETF flow\n  reversal would find no natural buyer beneath.\n- Insider activity: CEO option-exercise sales ~$76M (Feb), $18.7M (May), $101.9M\n  (Aug) [Estimate \u2014 Benzinga/Investing.com/MarketBeat]. Scale is a yellow flag,\n  though option exercises are diversification, not a directional dump.\n- Options positioning: [Unconfirmed \u2014 not retrieved]\n- Sentiment: sell-side mean target $198 (mean $198.06, high $230, low $170)\n  [Aggregator \u201